    && printf 'Ubuntu 24.04 amd64: exact canonical signed prior alpha.32 package verified by SHA-256; real APT installation, tampered package rejection with prior version retained, signed local repository upgrade to alpha.39 through the actual new updater helper, explicit pinned prior-package recovery and signed re-upgrade, preference checksum preservation, remove/reinstall, all four versions, helper ownership and non-root refusal, two actual cache cleanups and protected volume inspection on one administrator broker connection, current-version install refusal through broker, typed request rejection, EOF revocation and unknown request rejection, verified owner public anchor in the installed package, unprivileged offscreen startup, Cleaner GUI functional regression on Ubuntu 24.04 runtime, virtual X11 GUI shell including single startup-window check, actual root read-only volume metadata scan, non-root refusal and real X11 diagnostics, and isolated XFCE compositor setting readback passed. Actual installed Analyze-to-Boost GUI workflow with own-process memory only and receipt passed; installed research module, live keyless research/local follow-up/SQLite smoke (synthetic category; provider status in AI39-INSTALLED-RESEARCH.txt), no-key refusal and consent-off GUI checks passed. Disposable signing fixture for exact Alpha.32 to Alpha.39 upgrade. Owner trust anchor preserved; actual post-Boost read-only verification and native generated-marker fixture passed. Physical Mint acceptance and production signing remain pending.\n' > /home/tester/INSTALL-STATUS.txt



